{"title": "Sectional Mock #87 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A solid cone of radius 7 cm and height 7 cm was melted along with two solid spheres of radius 7 cm each to form a solid cylinder of radius 7 cm. what is the curved surface area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of the cylinder?</p><p>(user&#960; = 22/7)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 7cm &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 7cm &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; 7cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 7cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>(&#960; = 22/7 &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;)</p>", "options_en": ["2196", "924", "482", "880"], "options_hi": ["2196", "924", "482", "880"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of cone + volume of 2 spheres = volume of cylinder </p><p>1/3 * &#960; * 7<sup>2 </sup>* 7 + 2 * 4/3 * &#960; * 7<sup>3</sup> = &#960; * 7<sup>2 </sup>* height of cylinder </p><p>7/3 + 56/3 = height of cylinder </p><p>Height of cylinder = 21 cm</p><p>Therefore, curved surface area of cylinder = 2 * 22/7 * 7 * 21 = 924 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of cone + volume of 2 spheres = volume of cylinder </p><p>1/3 * &#960; * 7<sup>2 </sup>* 7 + 2 * 4/3 * &#960; * 7<sup>3</sup> = &#960; * 7<sup>2 </sup>* height of cylinder </p><p>7/3 + 56/3 = height of cylinder </p><p>Height of cylinder = 21 cm</p><p>Therefore, curved surface area of cylinder = 2 * 22/7 * 7 * 21 = 924 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If tan &#952; =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">7", "q_hi": "<p><div>&nbsp;&#2351;&#2342;&#2367;  tan &#952; =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">7", "options_en": ["2/5", "1/3", "4/5", "3/5"], "options_hi": ["2/5", "1/3", "4/5", "3/5"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>tan &#952; = 7/4</p><p>(4 sin &#952;  -  3)/(4 sin &#952; + 3 cos &#952;)</p><p>= (4 sin &#952;/cos &#952;  -  3 cos &#952;)/(4 sin &#952;/cos &#952; + 3)</p><p>= (4 tan &#952;  -  3)/(4 tan &#952; + 3)</p><p>= (4*7/4  -  3)/(4*7/4 + 3)</p><p>= (7  -  3)/(7 + 3)</p><p>= 4/10</p><p>= 2/5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>tan &#952; = 7/4</p><p>(4 sin &#952;  -  3)/(4 sin &#952; + 3 cos &#952;)</p><p>= (4 sin &#952;/cos &#952;  -  3 cos &#952;)/(4 sin &#952;/cos &#952; + 3)</p><p>= (4 tan &#952;  -  3)/(4 tan &#952; + 3)</p><p>= (4*7/4  -  3)/(4*7/4 + 3)</p><p>= (7  -  3)/(7 + 3)</p><p>= 4/10</p><p>= 2/5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum of &#8377;16,310 is to be repaid in 4 equal yearly installments of &#8377;3,500 each, starting after one year. If interest is charged at simple interest, what annual rate of interest is being applied?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>$16,310 &#2325;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; $3,500 &#2325;&#2368; 4 &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2342;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["10", "9", "11", "12"], "options_hi": ["10", "9", "11", "12"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>let the rate of interest be y.</p><p>Total interest = (3500 x y x 3/100) + (3500 x y x 2/100) + (3500 x y x 1/100) + (3500 x y x 0/100) = 210y</p><p>Total amount paid = 3500 x 4 + 210y = Rs.14000 + 210y</p><p>Given that,</p><p>14000 + 210y = 16310</p><p>210y = 2310</p><p>y=11%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>let the rate of interest be y.</p><p>Total interest = (3500 x y x 3/100) + (3500 x y x 2/100) + (3500 x y x 1/100) + (3500 x y x 0/100) = 210y</p><p>Total amount paid = 3500 x 4 + 210y = Rs.14000 + 210y</p><p>Given that,</p><p>14000 + 210y = 16310</p><p>210y = 2310</p><p>y=11%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>For what positive values of K do the following pair of linear equations have infinitely many solutions? </p><p>Kx + 9y  -  (K  -  9) = 0 </p><p>36x + Ky - K = 0 </p>", "q_hi": "<p>K &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2352;&#2376;&#2326;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2306;&#2340; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2375;&#2325; &#2361;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p><p>Kx + 9y - (K - 9) = 0 </p><p>36x + Ky - K = 0 </p>", "options_en": ["-9", "-12", "15", "18"], "options_hi": ["-9", "-12", "15", "18"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>A<sub>1</sub>x + B<sub>1</sub>y + C<sub>1</sub> = 0 .. (i)</p><p>A<sub>2</sub>x + B<sub>2</sub>Y + C<sub>2</sub> = 0 ... (ii)</p><p>If eq 1 and 2 have infinite solutions then, </p><p>A<sub>1</sub>/A<sub>2</sub> = B<sub>1</sub>/B<sub>2</sub> = C<sub>1</sub>/C<sub>2</sub> (Constant) </p><p>Kx + 9y  -  (K  -  9) = 0 </p><p>36x + Ky - K = 0 </p><p>A<sub>1</sub> = K, B<sub>1</sub> = 9, C<sub>1</sub> =  -  K + 9 ... (iii)</p><p>A<sub>2</sub> = 36, B<sub>2</sub> = K, C<sub>2</sub> = -K ... (iv)</p><p>K/36 = 9/K </p><p>K = 18, -18</p><p>9/K = (-K + 9)/-K </p><p>9 = K  -  9</p><p>K = 18</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A<sub>1</sub>x + B<sub>1</sub>y + C<sub>1</sub> = 0 .. (i)</p><p>A<sub>2</sub>x + B<sub>2</sub>Y + C<sub>2</sub> = 0 ... (ii)</p><p>If eq 1 and 2 have infinite solutions then, </p><p>A<sub>1</sub>/A<sub>2</sub> = B<sub>1</sub>/B<sub>2</sub> = C<sub>1</sub>/C<sub>2</sub> (Constant) </p><p>Kx + 9y  -  (K  -  9) = 0 </p><p>36x + Ky - K = 0 </p><p>A<sub>1</sub> = K, B<sub>1</sub> = 9, C<sub>1</sub> =  -  K + 9 ... (iii)</p><p>A<sub>2</sub> = 36, B<sub>2</sub> = K, C<sub>2</sub> = -K ... (iv)</p><p>K/36 = 9/K </p><p>K = 18, -18</p><p>9/K = (-K + 9)/-K </p><p>9 = K  -  9</p><p>K = 18</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Mohana and Rohan start travelling by their bikes simultaneously from place O to place P at the speed of 24 km/h and 36 km/hr, respectively. Rohan and Mohan reach the place P in T hours and (T + 1.6) hours, respectively. What is the distance between the place O and place P?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2379;&#2361;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2379;&#2361;&#2344; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 24 km/h &#2324;&#2352; 36 km/hr &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; O &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; P &#2340;&#2325; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; (&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352;) &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2352;&#2379;&#2361;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2379;&#2361;&#2344; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; P &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; T &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; (T + 1.6) &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2361;&#2369;&#2305;&#2330;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; O &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; P &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["122.6 km", "124.6 km", "110.2 km", "115.2 km"], "options_hi": ["122.6 km", "124.6 km", "110.2 km", "115.2 km"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>The time taken by Rohan to reach place P is T hours.</p><p>And the time taken by Mohan to reach place P is (T + 1.6) hours.</p><p>According to the question</p><p>=&gt; 24(T + 1.6) = 36 * T</p><p>=&gt; 24T + 38.4 = 36T</p><p>=&gt; 12T = 38.4 </p><p>=&gt; T = 3.2 hours</p><p>Now, distance between place O and place P = 24 * (3.2 + 1.6) = 115.2 km</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The time taken by Rohan to reach place P is T hours.</p><p>And the time taken by Mohan to reach place P is (T + 1.6) hours.</p><p>According to the question</p><p>=&gt; 24(T + 1.6) = 36 * T</p><p>=&gt; 24T + 38.4 = 36T</p><p>=&gt; 12T = 38.4 </p><p>=&gt; T = 3.2 hours</p><p>Now, distance between place O and place P = 24 * (3.2 + 1.6) = 115.2 km</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Aman used to spend 60% of his income and his income increased by 40% and his expenditure increased by 35%. If his initial savings were X and his new savings were Y, then find the value of 'X' is what percent more/less than Y. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2350;&#2344; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 60% &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 40% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 35% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; X &#2341;&#2368; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2312; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; Y &#2341;&#2368;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; 'X' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; Y &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;/&#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["42.5% more", "37.5% less", "47.5% less", "32.5% more"], "options_hi": ["42.5% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;", "37.5% &#2325;&#2350;", "47.5% &#2325;&#2350;", "32.5% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let Aman's initial income be Rs. '100'</p><p>Aman's initial expenditure = 100 * 60/100 = 60</p><p>Aman's initial saving = 100  -  60 = 40 </p><p>Aman's new income = 100 * 140/100 = 140 </p><p>Aman's new expenditure = 60 * 135/100 = 81 </p><p>Aman's new saving = 140  -  81 = 59 </p><p>Hence, [(Y  -  X) * 100/X] = [(59  -  40) * 100/40] = 47.5 less</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let Aman's initial income be Rs. '100'</p><p>Aman's initial expenditure = 100 * 60/100 = 60</p><p>Aman's initial saving = 100  -  60 = 40 </p><p>Aman's new income = 100 * 140/100 = 140 </p><p>Aman's new expenditure = 60 * 135/100 = 81 </p><p>Aman's new saving = 140  -  81 = 59 </p><p>Hence, [(Y  -  X) * 100/X] = [(59  -  40) * 100/40] = 47.5 less</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The value of 42.6 out of 1000 in decimal fraction is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1000 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 42.6 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["0.0426", "0.426", "0.00426", "4.26"], "options_hi": ["0.0426", "0.426", "0.00426", "4.26"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=124 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image001.png\"></p><p>= 5 + (32  -  3)/90  -  3  -  (25  -  2)/90 + 2 + (21  -  2)/90</p><p>= 4 + 29/90  -  23/90 + 19/90</p><p>= 385/90 = 77/18</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=124 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image001.png\"></p><p>= 5 + (32  -  3)/90  -  3  -  (25  -  2)/90 + 2 + (21  -  2)/90</p><p>= 4 + 29/90  -  23/90 + 19/90</p><p>= 385/90 = 77/18</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>In triangle ABC, D is the mid-point of BC. If DL perpendicular to AB and DM perpendicular to AC such that DL = DM, then the triangle will be:</p>", "q_hi": "&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, D, BC &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;-&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; DL, AB &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2357;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; DM, AC &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2357;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367; DL = DM &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;:", "options_en": ["isosceles triangle", "right angled triangle", "obtuse angle triangle", "equilateral triangle"], "options_hi": ["&#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332;", "&#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332;", "&#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332;", "&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>In a triangle, if the perpendiculars drawn from the mid-point of one side to the other two sides are equal, then the triangle is isosceles.</p><p>Given DL = DM and D is the mid-point of BC, it implies that triangle ABD is congruent to triangle ACD by RHS (Right angle-Hypotenuse-Side) congruence.</p><p>Since triangle ABD &#8773; triangle ACD, it implies that AB = AC.</p><p>Hence, triangle ABC is an isosceles triangle.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In a triangle, if the perpendiculars drawn from the mid-point of one side to the other two sides are equal, then the triangle is isosceles.</p><p>Given DL = DM and D is the mid-point of BC, it implies that triangle ABD is congruent to triangle ACD by RHS (Right angle-Hypotenuse-Side) congruence.</p><p>Since triangle ABD &#8773; triangle ACD, it implies that AB = AC.</p><p>Hence, triangle ABC is an isosceles triangle.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A man buys some quantity of milk at &#8377;90 per litre. He sold one litre of milk to Uday and Rachit each at 100/litre. He sold 950 ml to Uday and 800 ml to Rachit instead of one litre using false weight. Find the profit made by selling the milk to Uday and Rachit together.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2342;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#8377;90 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2366;&#2348; &#2360;&#2375; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2313;&#2342;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325;-&#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; 100/&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2366;&#2348; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2311;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2375;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; &#2313;&#2342;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 950 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; 800 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;&#2404; &#2313;&#2342;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;42.5", "&#8377;36.5", "&#8377;45.5", "&#8377;32.5"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;42.5", "&#8377;36.5", "&#8377;45.5", "&#8377;32.5"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Cost price of milk = &#8377;90/kg</p><p>Selling price of Uday and Rachit each = &#8377;100/kg</p><p>Total profit = 2(100  -  90) + (1000  -  950)*90/1000 + (1000  -  800)*90/1000</p><p>= 20 + 2.5*9 </p><p>= 20 + 22.5</p><p>= &#8377;42.5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Cost price of milk = &#8377;90/kg</p><p>Selling price of Uday and Rachit each = &#8377;100/kg</p><p>Total profit = 2(100  -  90) + (1000  -  950)*90/1000 + (1000  -  800)*90/1000</p><p>= 20 + 2.5*9 </p><p>= 20 + 22.5</p><p>= &#8377;42.5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>The time 't' to go over a fixed distance is in reverse proportion to the average speed 'v' of the vehicle. When the average speed of the vehicle is 50 km/hr it takes 6 hours to go over a certain distance. Find the time (in hrs) required to cover the same distance at an average speed of 60 km/hr?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; 'T' &#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 'V' &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2354;&#2335;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 50 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; 60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["2.5", "4", "6", "5"], "options_hi": ["2.5", "4", "6", "5"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>t &prop; 1/v or t = k/v </p><p>6 = k/50 or k = 300</p><p>At 60 km/hr, t = 300/60 = 5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>t &prop; 1/v or t = k/v </p><p>6 = k/50 or k = 300</p><p>At 60 km/hr, t = 300/60 = 5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>A man invested an amount of Rs. 105750 at simple interest in the name of his son, daughter and his wife in such a way that they get the same interest after 3, 4 and 5 years, respectively. If the rate of interest is 5% per annum, then the amount invested for the wife is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;, &#2346;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2340;&#2381;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2366;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; 105750 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2311;&#2360; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;: 3, 4 &#2324;&#2352; 5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; 5% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2340;&#2381;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; _______ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 30000", "Rs. 28000", "Rs. 25000", "Rs. 27000"], "options_hi": ["30000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "28000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "25000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "27000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Total amount = Rs. 105750</p><p>Let the amount invested for the son, daughter and wife = P<sub>1</sub>, P<sub>2</sub>, P<sub>3</sub></p><p>R = 5%</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>P<sub>1</sub> * 3 * 5/100 = P<sub>2</sub> * 4 * 5/100 = P<sub>3</sub> * 5 * 5/100</p><p>3P<sub>1</sub> = 4P<sub>2</sub> = 5P<sub>3</sub></p><p>Since, P<sub>1</sub> + P<sub>2</sub> + P<sub>3</sub> = 105750</p><p>5P<sub>3</sub>/3 + 5P<sub>3</sub>/4 + P<sub>3</sub> = 105750</p><p>47P<sub>3</sub>/12 = 105750</p><p>P<sub>3 </sub>= 105750 * 12/47</p><p>P<sub>3 </sub>= Rs. 27000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total amount = Rs. 105750</p><p>Let the amount invested for the son, daughter and wife = P<sub>1</sub>, P<sub>2</sub>, P<sub>3</sub></p><p>R = 5%</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>P<sub>1</sub> * 3 * 5/100 = P<sub>2</sub> * 4 * 5/100 = P<sub>3</sub> * 5 * 5/100</p><p>3P<sub>1</sub> = 4P<sub>2</sub> = 5P<sub>3</sub></p><p>Since, P<sub>1</sub> + P<sub>2</sub> + P<sub>3</sub> = 105750</p><p>5P<sub>3</sub>/3 + 5P<sub>3</sub>/4 + P<sub>3</sub> = 105750</p><p>47P<sub>3</sub>/12 = 105750</p><p>P<sub>3 </sub>= 105750 * 12/47</p><p>P<sub>3 </sub>= Rs. 27000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>If x<sup>4</sup> + y<sup>4</sup>+x<sup>2</sup>y<sup>2</sup> = 21 and x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>  -  xy = 7, then what is the value of (x/y) + (y/x)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x<sup>4</sup> + y<sup>4</sup>+x<sup>2</sup>y<sup>2</sup> = 21 &#2324;&#2352; x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup> - xy = 7 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (x/y) + (y/x) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["5/4", "3/4", "-3/2", "-5/2"], "options_hi": ["5/4", "3/4", "-3/2", "-5/2"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>x<sup>4</sup> + y<sup>4</sup>+x<sup>2</sup>y<sup>2</sup> = 21</p><p>and x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>  -  xy = 7--------(1)</p><p>x<sup>4</sup> + y<sup>4</sup>+x<sup>2</sup>y<sup>2</sup>= (x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>  -  xy)(x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>+xy)</p><p>21 = 7 * (x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>+xy)</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup> + xy =3 ------(2)</p><p>From eq(1) and eq(2)  - </p><p>x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>=5 and xy = -2</p><p>So, (x/y) + (y/x) = (x<sup>2</sup>+y<sup>2</sup>)/xy=5/(-2)</p><p>= -5/2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x<sup>4</sup> + y<sup>4</sup>+x<sup>2</sup>y<sup>2</sup> = 21</p><p>and x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>  -  xy = 7--------(1)</p><p>x<sup>4</sup> + y<sup>4</sup>+x<sup>2</sup>y<sup>2</sup>= (x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>  -  xy)(x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>+xy)</p><p>21 = 7 * (x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>+xy)</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup> + xy =3 ------(2)</p><p>From eq(1) and eq(2)  - </p><p>x<sup>2</sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>=5 and xy = -2</p><p>So, (x/y) + (y/x) = (x<sup>2</sup>+y<sup>2</sup>)/xy=5/(-2)</p><p>= -5/2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p><b>Direction:</b>   The following histogram shows the data collected by a weighing machine in terms of number of people according to their weight who weighs themselves on the machine in a day.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18239/image004.png\"></p><p>The ratio of number of people who weigh 65 kg or more to the number of people who weigh 45 kg or more, but less than 55 kg is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p><b>&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342;&#2375;&#2358;:</b> &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2350;&#2358;&#2368;&#2344; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2310;&#2305;&#2325;&#2396;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2358;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18239/image004.png\"></p><p>65 kg &#2351;&#2366; &#2313;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 45 kg &#2351;&#2366; &#2313;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; 55 kg &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["2: 3", "1: 3", "3: 2", "2: 1"], "options_hi": ["2: 3", "1: 3", "3: 2", "2: 1"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>The number of people who weigh 65 kg or more = 12 + 10 + 5 = 27</p><p>The number of people who weigh 45 kg or more, but less than 55 kg = 8 + 10 = 18</p><p>Required ratio = 27: 18 = 3: 2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The number of people who weigh 65 kg or more = 12 + 10 + 5 = 27</p><p>The number of people who weigh 45 kg or more, but less than 55 kg = 8 + 10 = 18</p><p>Required ratio = 27: 18 = 3: 2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the number of trailing zeros in 1000!  X  1500!.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1000! X 1500! &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2358;&#2370;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["622", "623", "624", "621"], "options_hi": ["622", "623", "624", "621"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>1000! zeros = 1000 mod 5 + 1000 mod 25 + 1000 mod 125 + 1000 mod 625</p><p>= 200 + 40 + 8 + 1 = 249</p><p>1500! zeros = 1500 mod 5 + 1500 mod 25 + 1500 mod 125 + 1500 mod 625</p><p>= 300 + 60 + 12 + 2 = 374</p><p>Combined = 249 + 374 = 623</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>1000! zeros = 1000 mod 5 + 1000 mod 25 + 1000 mod 125 + 1000 mod 625</p><p>= 200 + 40 + 8 + 1 = 249</p><p>1500! zeros = 1500 mod 5 + 1500 mod 25 + 1500 mod 125 + 1500 mod 625</p><p>= 300 + 60 + 12 + 2 = 374</p><p>Combined = 249 + 374 = 623</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A, B and C enters into partnership for 1 year with investment in the ratio 2 : 3 : 5. If difference between annual profit of B and C is Rs. 8000. Find the annual profit of A.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2324;&#2352; C 2: 3: 5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; 1 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2352;&#2369;. 8000 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 10,600", "Rs. 10,000", "Rs. 8000", "Rs. 6000"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 10,600", "&#2352;&#2369;. 10,000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 8000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 6000"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the investment of A, B and C be 2x, 3x and 5x respectively.</p><p>According to question, </p><p>5x  -  3x = Rs. 8000</p><p>2x = Rs. 8000 </p><p>x = Rs. 4000</p><p>Annual Profit of A = 2 * 4000 = Rs. 8000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the investment of A, B and C be 2x, 3x and 5x respectively.</p><p>According to question, </p><p>5x  -  3x = Rs. 8000</p><p>2x = Rs. 8000 </p><p>x = Rs. 4000</p><p>Annual Profit of A = 2 * 4000 = Rs. 8000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>If sin{3(x - y)} = cos(x - y), then what is the value of tan{2(x  -  y)}?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; sin{3(x - y)} = cos(x - y) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; tan{2(x - y)} &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1", "&radic;3", "1/&radic;3", "0"], "options_hi": ["1", "&radic;3", "1/&radic;3", "0"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>sin{3(x - y)} = cos(x - y)</p><p>cos{90 - 3(x - y)} = cos(x - y)</p><p>90  -  3(x  -  y) = x  -  y</p><p>2(x  -  y) = 45&deg;</p><p>tan{2(x  -  y)} = tan45&deg; = 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>sin{3(x - y)} = cos(x - y)</p><p>cos{90 - 3(x - y)} = cos(x - y)</p><p>90  -  3(x  -  y) = x  -  y</p><p>2(x  -  y) = 45&deg;</p><p>tan{2(x  -  y)} = tan45&deg; = 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of the incomes of Keshav and Ratan in the last year was 8:9. The ratio of their individual incomes in the last year and the present year are 6:7 and 3:4 respectively. If their total income in the present year is &#8377;15.36 lakhs, then what is the sum of the income (in lakhs) of Keshav in the last year and that of Ratan in the present year?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375;&#2358;&#2357; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 8:9 &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2327;&#2340; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 6:7 &#2324;&#2352; 3:4 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2310;&#2351; 15.36 &#2354;&#2366;&#2326; &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375;&#2358;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; (&#2354;&#2366;&#2326;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["14.4", "18.5", "13.2", "21.25"], "options_hi": ["14.4", "18.5", "13.2", "21.25"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the income of Keshav and Ratan in the last year was &#8377;8p and &#8377;9p respectively.</p><p>Total income of Keshav in the present year = 8p*7/6 = 28p/3</p><p>Total income of Ratan in the present year = 9p*4/3 = 12p</p><p>Now,</p><p>28p/3 + 12p = 15.36 lakh</p><p>64p/3 = 15.36</p><p>p = 72000</p><p>Sum of the income of Keshav in the last year and that of Ratan in the present year = 8*72000 + 12*72000 = 14.4 lakhs</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the income of Keshav and Ratan in the last year was &#8377;8p and &#8377;9p respectively.</p><p>Total income of Keshav in the present year = 8p*7/6 = 28p/3</p><p>Total income of Ratan in the present year = 9p*4/3 = 12p</p><p>Now,</p><p>28p/3 + 12p = 15.36 lakh</p><p>64p/3 = 15.36</p><p>p = 72000</p><p>Sum of the income of Keshav in the last year and that of Ratan in the present year = 8*72000 + 12*72000 = 14.4 lakhs</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the volume in cubic units of a cylinder with a height equal to the diameter and a radius is 4 units?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2328;&#2344; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 4 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;?", "options_en": ["128&#960;", "64&#960;/3", "32&#960;", "32&#960;/3"], "options_hi": ["128&#960;", "64&#960;/3", "32&#960;", "32&#960;/3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of a cylinder = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h</p><p>Height (h) = 2  X  Radius = 2  X  4 = 8 units</p><p>Volume = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h</p><p>=&gt; &#960;  X  4<sup>2</sup>  X  8 = 128&#960;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of a cylinder = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h</p><p>Height (h) = 2  X  Radius = 2  X  4 = 8 units</p><p>Volume = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h</p><p>=&gt; &#960;  X  4<sup>2</sup>  X  8 = 128&#960;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the sum of five consecutive even natural numbers is 260, then the middle number is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 260 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["50", "52", "48", "54"], "options_hi": ["50", "52", "48", "54"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the middle number be 'a'</p><p>The sum of five consecutive even numbers = 260</p><p>(a  -  4) + (a  -  2) + a + (a + 2) + (a + 4) = 260</p><p>5a = 260</p><p>a = 52</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the middle number be 'a'</p><p>The sum of five consecutive even numbers = 260</p><p>(a  -  4) + (a  -  2) + a + (a + 2) + (a + 4) = 260</p><p>5a = 260</p><p>a = 52</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A train running at 72 km/h crosses a pole in 12 seconds. How much time (in seconds) will it take to cross a bridge 360 m long?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; 12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 360 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2346;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["40", "75", "60", "30"], "options_hi": ["40", "75", "60", "30"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Speed of train = 72 kmph = 72 * 5/18 = 20 m/s</p><p>Distance covered in 12 second = 20 * 12 = 240 m</p><p>Required time = (240 + 360)/20 = 600/20 = 30 sec</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Speed of train = 72 kmph = 72 * 5/18 = 20 m/s</p><p>Distance covered in 12 second = 20 * 12 = 240 m</p><p>Required time = (240 + 360)/20 = 600/20 = 30 sec</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup> = 83, then find the value of (x<sup>2</sup>  -  1)/x?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup> = 83, &#2340;&#2379; (x<sup>2</sup> - 1)/x &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["&#177;11", "&#177;3", "&#177;9", "&#177;5"], "options_hi": ["&#177;11", "&#177;3", "&#177;9", "&#177;5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup> = 83</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup>  -  2 = 83 - 2</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup>  -  2 = 81</p><p>(x  -  1/x)<sup>2</sup> = 81</p><p>x  -  1/x = &#177;9</p><p>(x<sup>2</sup>  -  1)/x = &#177;9</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup> = 83</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup>  -  2 = 83 - 2</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup>  -  2 = 81</p><p>(x  -  1/x)<sup>2</sup> = 81</p><p>x  -  1/x = &#177;9</p><p>(x<sup>2</sup>  -  1)/x = &#177;9</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A ship can travel 8 km upstream and 15 km downstream in 42 min. If ratio of speed of ship in still water to the speed of stream is 7: 3, then find the time taken to cover 12 km upstream and 20 km downstream together.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2332; 42 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; 8 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 15 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 7:3 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 12 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 20 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["0.8 hour", "1.2 hours", "1 hour", "1.5 hour"], "options_hi": ["0.8 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "1.2 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "1 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "1.5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let speed of ship in still water and speed of stream be '7x' and '3x' respectively.</p><p>Upstream speed of ship = 7x  -  3x = 4x</p><p>Downstream speed of ship = 7x + 3x = 10x</p><p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=101 height=73 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11800/image011.png\"></p><p>x = 5</p><p>Upstream speed of ship = 4x = 20 km/h</p><p>Downstream speed of ship = 10x = 50 km/h</p><p>Required time = <img width=132 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11800/image012.png\"></p><p>= 1 hour</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let speed of ship in still water and speed of stream be '7x' and '3x' respectively.</p><p>Upstream speed of ship = 7x  -  3x = 4x</p><p>Downstream speed of ship = 7x + 3x = 10x</p><p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=101 height=73 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11800/image011.png\"></p><p>x = 5</p><p>Upstream speed of ship = 4x = 20 km/h</p><p>Downstream speed of ship = 10x = 50 km/h</p><p>Required time = <img width=132 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11800/image012.png\"></p><p>= 1 hour</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the number of trailing zeros in 308!?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>308 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2358;&#2370;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["80", "68", "75", "92"], "options_hi": ["80", "68", "75", "92"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Number of zeroes = number of pairs of 2 * 5</p><p>Quotient of 308/5 = 61</p><p>Quotient of 61/5 = 12</p><p>Quotient of 12/5 = 2</p><p>Total number of zeroes = 61 + 12 + 2 = 75</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of zeroes = number of pairs of 2 * 5</p><p>Quotient of 308/5 = 61</p><p>Quotient of 61/5 = 12</p><p>Quotient of 12/5 = 2</p><p>Total number of zeroes = 61 + 12 + 2 = 75</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper increases the marked price of rice by 25% above the cost price and offers a certain discount to customers. He uses a false weight, giving 900 gm instead of 1 kg. If his total profit percentage is 33.33%, then find the discount percentage he provides on the marked price.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 25% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; 900 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; 33.33% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4%", "7%", "2.5%", "3%"], "options_hi": ["4%", "7%", "2.5%", "3%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let cost price of 1000 gm of rice = &#8377;100</p><p>Marked price of rice = 125% of 100 = &#8377;125</p><p>Cost price of 900 gm = &#8377;90</p><p>Profit percentage = 33.33% = 1/3</p><p>Selling price of rice = (1 + 1/3)*90 = &#8377;120</p><p>Discount = 100  -  (120/125)*100 = 4%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let cost price of 1000 gm of rice = &#8377;100</p><p>Marked price of rice = 125% of 100 = &#8377;125</p><p>Cost price of 900 gm = &#8377;90</p><p>Profit percentage = 33.33% = 1/3</p><p>Selling price of rice = (1 + 1/3)*90 = &#8377;120</p><p>Discount = 100  -  (120/125)*100 = 4%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>If p = (1  -  Tan<sup>2</sup>B) and q = (1  -  Cot<sup>2</sup>B), then the expression [1  -  (p/q)] = ?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; p = (1 - Tan<sup>2</sup>B) &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; q = (1 - Cot<sup>2</sup>B) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2349;&#2367;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; [1 - (p/q)] = ? &#2361;&#2376;-</p>", "options_en": ["Sec<sup>2</sup>B + 1", "1  -  Tan<sup>2</sup>B", "Sec<sup>2</sup>B", "Tan<sup>2</sup>B"], "options_hi": ["Sec<sup>2</sup>B + 1", "1 - Tan<sup>2</sup>B", "Sec<sup>2</sup>B", "Tan<sup>2</sup>B"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>p = (1  -  Tan<sup>2</sup>B) and q = (1  -  Cot<sup>2</sup>B)</p><p>p = (Cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>B)/Cos<sup>2</sup>B</p><p>q =  - (Cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>B)/ Sin<sup>2</sup>B</p><p>p/q = [(Cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>B)/Cos<sup>2</sup>B]/[  - (Cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>B)/ Sin<sup>2</sup>B]</p><p>p/q =  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>B/ Cos<sup>2</sup>B =  - Tan<sup>2</sup>B</p><p>1  -  (p/q) = 1 + Tan<sup>2</sup>B = Sec<sup>2</sup>B</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>p = (1  -  Tan<sup>2</sup>B) and q = (1  -  Cot<sup>2</sup>B)</p><p>p = (Cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>B)/Cos<sup>2</sup>B</p><p>q =  - (Cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>B)/ Sin<sup>2</sup>B</p><p>p/q = [(Cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>B)/Cos<sup>2</sup>B]/[  - (Cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>B)/ Sin<sup>2</sup>B]</p><p>p/q =  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>B/ Cos<sup>2</sup>B =  - Tan<sup>2</sup>B</p><p>1  -  (p/q) = 1 + Tan<sup>2</sup>B = Sec<sup>2</sup>B</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}]}